; guardprobe -- a FIXTURE, not a lang.
;
; tools/check/wrapper.sh starts an interactive session with this bundle on a
; pty and asks whether its entry ran with no guard around it.  A lang's REPL
; relies on that: the engine raises STOP on a ctrl-c only while a guard is
; active, so a lang's own handler for an interrupted read runs with the flag
; still set, and a guard outside the session would take that STOP and end it.
;
; helium: the cheapest dialect that boots.

(lang "guardprobe")
(dialect he)
(entry "run.x")
